DevRounds executor

This workspace contains code copied from devlanes
(https://github.com/devlanes-run/devlanes), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). Every copied crate was taken at commit
e2e4f1cafda94805d6e447331980b83fcbab2e72 and renamed from devlanes-* to
devrounds-*; upstream names of types and functions are kept so later ports stay
mechanical. devlanes-sync.toml records the crates and the upstream commits
reviewed since.

Upstream READMEs and CHANGELOGs were not copied. Copied tests were kept where
they still apply; temporary directories moved from the system temp to Cargo's
target directory.

Changes per crate
-----------------

devrounds-core, from crates/core at e2e4f1cafda94805d6e447331980b83fcbab2e72
  Kept clock, gate, runtime, stop. paths keeps only names_a_path and fold_case;
  env keeps only fold_name. Removed color, contrib, ports, redact, refs, the
  lane/project/unit-run ids and Actor. runtime drops pseudo-terminal launches
  (LaunchSpec pty/size, TerminalSize, OutputStream::Terminal), Power, ExitSweep
  and the Unit methods input, resize, set_power and renders_screen.
  ProcessInfo moved here from devlanes-sys. StartRequest is
  { run, job_type, order, memory_need } instead of lane/unit, and
  GateSnapshot::find takes a run id. Added DrError (error.rs) and JobSpec
  (job.rs).

devrounds-sys-windows, from crates/sys-windows at e2e4f1cafda94805d6e447331980b83fcbab2e72
  Removed cert, conpty, net, pipe, power, registry and shell_execute with their
  tests and windows-sys features, the test-support feature and rcgen.
  Removed Job::adopt_suspended (needed power), the Stdio::PseudoConsole spawn
  path (needed conpty), security::kernel_object_owner and util::hresult_error,
  which only the removed modules used, and the proc TCP table wrappers
  (listening_tcp, tcp_listeners, established_tcp) with the IpHelper and
  WinSock windows-sys features; only listening_ports used them. Window class
  and title are devrounds names.

devrounds-shell-windows, from crates/shell-windows at e2e4f1cafda94805d6e447331980b83fcbab2e72
  Removed exec_path_root, which started `git --exec-path` through
  tokio::process outside devrounds_sys_windows::spawn; windows_shell now finds
  Git's sh.exe from PATH only.

devrounds-runner-windows, from crates/runner-windows at e2e4f1cafda94805d6e447331980b83fcbab2e72
  Removed foreground (spawn_foreground, shell_exit_code), terminal (ConPTY
  units, batch-prompt answers), listening_ports, set_power/freezing,
  with_exit_sweep and the devlanes-sys dependency. output.rs is kept without
  terminal sizing until run output moves to run-owned files. The integration
  tests that drove devlanes-testing's fixture-server (stops, orphans, process
  trees, freezing, throttling) and the pseudo-console tests were not copied;
  the cmd and sh.exe tests were.

devrounds-start-gate, from crates/start-gate at e2e4f1cafda94805d6e447331980b83fcbab2e72
  Requests carry run and job_type instead of lane and unit.

devrounds-metrics, from crates/metrics at e2e4f1cafda94805d6e447331980b83fcbab2e72
  Kept ring, sketch and run. Removed aggregate and history. The subject of a
  sample is a run id: Subject is Run, Process (with run) or Daemon; UnitKey,
  container, Docker VM, project and lane subjects are gone. RunTracker and
  RunSummary are keyed by run id.

devrounds-metrics-windows, from crates/metrics-windows at e2e4f1cafda94805d6e447331980b83fcbab2e72
  Samples carry the run id of their target instead of a unit key. Container
  targets are gone from SampleRequest and its tests.

devrounds-logs, from crates/logs at e2e4f1cafda94805d6e447331980b83fcbab2e72
  Kept framing, level and storage. Removed query and the grep-* and jiff
  dependencies. LogLine moved into this crate from devlanes-proto (not
  copied) with its unit field renamed to run. LogReader lost its unused unit
  field and storage its unused skip helper, which only query read. Tests
  use expect instead of allowing clippy::unwrap_used; the query-based tests
  were dropped.

Not copied: devlanes-sys (only ProcessInfo was needed), devlanes-proto (only
LogLine was needed) and devlanes-runner-pty
(Unix-only; Windows terminals wait for a later phase).
